WEBVTT

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:25.180
I would describe Lita as the most natural, sexy, athletic woman in the WWF.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:29.510
I just always looked at her as someone that reminded me of a female Hardy.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.140
she was willing to try things that others may want to shy away from and there was never any moves that

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:41.760
she was intimidated to attempt. Lita loves wrestling, her heart is totally into wrestling and

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:49.180
I think she's just going to continue to surprise people with new ideas and new things and continue

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:56.230
to be great. She's sexy and she's risky and she's extreme and I think that appeals to you know both

00:00:56.230 --> 00:01:00.000
sexes, and I think it's great that a diva and someone, you know, a

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.280
sex symbol-ish woman can represent that

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.080
yet go out there and be athletic and do what she does

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.120
I think Lita's definitely a pioneer

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.560
she's a different animal from a lot of the other girls

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.460
but if you were going to

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.100
weigh out everyone's strengths and weaknesses

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.360
I think Lita would rank up there

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.480
right at the top of the pack

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.540
and Lita can wrestle and she can wrestle

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.320
like no other woman can wrestle right now

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:21.550
Algo

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:25.480
an energy that makes you vibrate and

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.390
make you feel, it was something incredible

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:30.000
the first time I was with her, it was something different but

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:35.050
a la vez, espontaneo, fue algo maravilloso.

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:37.430
In every business, there's going to be a formula.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:41.870
I believe to be successful in this business, you have to at least know about it, because

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:46.320
there's formulas for a reason, but at the same time, when you're branching out and doing

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.340
something new, going down roads that haven't been traveled before, you're kind of creating

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.120
them as you go along, so you've got to kind of see what's worked in the past and add your

00:01:55.120 --> 00:02:00.000
own elements to that, pour everything into one pot and stir it around and kind of jump

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:01.960
and see what you get out of it.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:18.900
say there's a you know a lot of athletic ability required to get in the

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:22.440
ring but at the same time there's a big level of commitment that you have to have

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:28.450
to driving around and going and getting beat up and getting hurt got a question

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.000
a lot of times for what

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:41.410
Because you don't know that your timing will ever be right to where you get that opportunity.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:45.410
So it takes a strange breed. We're all a strange breed and I think we'd admit that. If it's

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:50.030
not in your heart, you're not going to make it because it can be pretty rough sometimes.

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:54.790
But at the end, looking back, or even now, just sitting here, being in the middle of

00:03:54.790 --> 00:04:00.000
it, you know, you know it's worth it. Like we say, you know, you're going to have to

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.860
living your dream you can't think of anything else you'd rather be doing it.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:16.750
Growing up I was always really independent as I still am. My mom was

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:20.450
always there for guidance whatever I needed. If I wanted to go to her she was

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:23.730
always kind of giving me the space I needed to try new stuff out. I was always

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:28.850
athletic growing up. My first taste of that was being on the swim team. I was on

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:30.000
the swim team since

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.360
I could remember, probably five years old.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.340
As I started getting into wrestling, actually,

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:36.900
I started Muay Thai kickboxing for a little while,

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.720
but I also did judo, and that was something I really got into,

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.560
and I started competing with that all over the East Coast,

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.780
and I learned a lot from there about competition,

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:47.340
which I think is really what has helped me here.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.640
We're all part of a big show. We're all working together,

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.720
but at the same time, it's that competition in your heart

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:55.110
that drives you to really, you know, get it out there when you need to.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:59.860
Once they started integrating the Mexicans into the American wrestling,

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.940
That's really what got me hooked.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:05.140
The style was just really different and really acrobatic,

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:07.640
so that's how I started watching.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.440
I didn't take long from there once I was watching

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:12.600
to kind of stay on the couch after the Mexicans

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:15.620
had done their segment and then really kind of get pulled

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:18.300
into the storylines, which is why I think a lot of us

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:19.820
are so intrigued by it.

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:22.040
You want to wait and see what happens,

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.580
make sure that person gets revenge.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:26.150
And that's what initially got me hooked.

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:27.810
It's really very much a characteristic

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:29.860
of my personality, where if something

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:36.140
sounds kind of neat to me. Without overanalyzing it, I'll just go for it. And maybe an hour

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:40.800
later or maybe six months later, it might not seem so cool to me, but nonetheless, I

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:46.020
will have had the experience for it. That was one of those things with Mexico and wrestling

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:50.870
where it just kind of clicked. That seems like it'd be really cool to do. And I never

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:55.300
really thought much beyond that, other than making travel arrangements and stuff to go

00:05:55.300 --> 00:06:00.000
down there. And if I hated it, it was the worst experience of my life. At least it was

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.700
more experience in my life that i had had so unfortunately it was the best experience of my

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:11.700
life at that time absorbing their culture and their way of life and then to watch the matches

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:16.500
and to talk with some of the wrestlers there that was a really you know positive business experience

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:22.880
this is a really unique culture that i've never been around until now and it's really

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:26.970
being so submerged in it i fell in love with it almost instantly after i got over

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:30.000
the initial culture shock it really kept me motivated to do everything

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:31.280
I could to get here.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:33.990
I was fortunate enough to see a couple mask

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:35.950
versus mask matches there.

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:38.230
A really big deal. Those would be

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:39.830
like at a SummerSlam or WrestleMania

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:42.090
pay-per-view. So when I first got there, I was just

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:43.970
buying every mask I could see,

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.950
whatever looked the coolest, you know, my favorite

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:48.110
ones, or people that I had met down there.

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:50.070
So it's actually like I'm looking at people

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:52.060
when I see them. We're in my kitchen

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:54.080
right now, and I wanted to show you guys

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.920
all the masks I got in Mexico.

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:57.720
Actually, it's not all of them.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.000
But we have a little park,

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:09.220
Riley Jalisco, and he beat Val Venus' ass and took his mask off him when I saw him.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:17.380
And then Psychosis and Scorpio Jr., he's shy, he's turned the other way.

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:22.250
I forget the guy's name, Mysterioso, that's his name.

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:28.050
Ray Mysterio Jr., and then at the end is Steel, it's Val Venus in Mexico.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.000
And across the way, there's their buddies.

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:39.790
square to Guerrero, that one in the middle.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:43.790
In the States, the facial expressions are what the people need to see.

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:48.010
But there, it's almost they like the mystery, not knowing what's underneath the mask and

00:07:48.010 --> 00:07:51.160
just seeing it almost as more of a superhero.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:04.900
I remember being on the Indies and I was lucky enough to have a little group of friends to

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:05.900
travel with.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:10.300
We tried to get ourselves booked on shows, but we would have really crazy loops from

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:15.820
when you would start your first show to the end, basically revolving around the weekend.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:22.220
Thursday night in Baltimore, and Friday night in North Carolina, Saturday night in Tennessee,

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:24.930
and Sunday night back in Baltimore.

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:26.480
I mean, that's what made it fun.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:30.000
I don't know how long you can keep up with that because you're not paid much to begin

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:34.000
by trying to put gas in your tank, you're back at negative.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:36.970
It's a good challenge to try to make your money last

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:39.590
and to try to be very creative as to how

00:08:39.590 --> 00:08:45.100
to fulfill your dream but survive at the same time.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:47.440
I was at ECW for about five months.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:49.540
I had some shows in North Carolina.

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:53.100
And I did my usual routine of if I wasn't booked on the show,

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:56.140
showing up anyways, and just smiling real big.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:09:00.000
And I introduced myself to Tommy Dreamer and asked if I could possibly

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:03.680
work out with the guys or watch and just learn something.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:07.870
I said, "Sure, you know, we're about to get ready for the show, but if you come back tomorrow,

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:12.150
you know, maybe you can work out with them, possibly have a little match or something."

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:16.330
I came back the next day and, super crazy, and Tajiri were there, I remember.

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:21.640
And Tajiri worked in Mexico when I was down there, so I went over and talked to him a little bit.

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:25.740
He actually started working out, and they came over and said, "You know, if you can get

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:30.000
together a little five-minute match, you can have a little tryout match." And from there, they said,

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.000
"Okay, you can work on the show tonight."

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.710
It was like, "Wow, okay, cool."

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:38.960
I got to take a pile driver at the end of the match

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:40.920
and lay there.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:42.940
You know, I was kind of just really laying low

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:46.040
for most of my time there, not really doing much,

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:48.380
just kind of keeping my eyes open.

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:49.880
And actually, it wasn't until right about

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:51.520
when I was getting ready to leave

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:54.200
that I really kind of started to feel more in touch

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:56.200
with the Miss Congeniality character

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:57.560
that they've given me over there.

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:06.740
One of my first memories beginning my journey here at the WWF was a meeting to possibly

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:07.720
work here.

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:10.250
I went out and I bought this suit.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:15.420
Like, I've never worn a suit in my life, but I'm like, oh, I'm going out this business

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:16.420
meeting.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:20.500
You know, they just sat there and talked to me for about, you know, 15, 20 minutes or

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:21.500
so.

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:24.440
And I remember Jim Ross said, all right, well, honey, I don't see any reason why we shouldn't

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:30.000
just sign up for a little developmental deal right now.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:31.610
So it was good to me.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:34.900
She was very positive about where she thought she could go

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:40.780
and was willing to come to work for the opportunity to be a part of the WWF.

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:42.740
So I thought I was impressed with that.

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:44.960
So from there, I finished up with ECW.

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:47.990
Right about at the end of 99, I started coming up

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:52.050
and just did some preliminary stuff, getting ready, taking some pictures.

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:54.770
And they told me about the idea of putting me with SA.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:57.710
I noticed this big, giant tattoo on her shoulder,

00:10:57.850 --> 00:11:00.000
and she asked me to watch what she did that night.

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:06.680
Subsequently, I did, and sooner or later, I saw Lita debut with Eze Rios and do these

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:12.470
incredible high-flying maneuvers, and I was just very, very impressed with her athleticism.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:30.000
He was just very charismatic, and he was really...

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:34.830
just into wrestling he was one of the top guys down there at the top so when they talked about

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:40.190
putting me with him that was really exciting but in wrestling as i'm sure with a lot of other things

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:44.750
everything changes up until you head out the curtain you know i remember when we started

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:50.900
it was kind of an impromptu thing one of the writers came over real late that afternoon and

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:56.170
said all right you guys are up tonight that was it it kind of shot down the starters

00:11:56.170 --> 00:12:00.000
some glitch in somebody else's storyline allowed me an essay to go out and

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.700
work that night.

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:05.640
Well, baby, tonight I'm putting out an open challenge to any light heavyweight in that

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:09.610
locker room that thinks he can beat me, because there ain't one.

